Excellent! This confirms my understanding:
- bash (pid 27071) is the test.sh
- `sleep 30` (pid 27073) — child of bash, has its own pgid (27073) and sid (27073) — this is the `setsid sleep 30` grandchild
- `sleep 60` (pid 27074) — child of bash, shares the parent's pgid (27066)
- The grandchild's ppid is 27071 (the bash), so BFS via ppid will find it

The proc stat layout: `pid (comm) state ppid pgrp session ...`
- After the last `)`: `S 27066 27066 27066 0 -1 4194304 671 0 ...`
- Fields after `)`: 0=state, 1=ppid, 2=pgrp, 3=session

So to parse ppid:
```js
const line = fs.readFileSync(`/proc/${pid}/stat`, 'utf8').trim();
const lastParen = line.lastIndexOf(')');
const after = line.slice(lastParen + 1).trim();
const tokens = after.split(/\s+/);
// tokens[0] = state, tokens[1] = ppid
const ppid = Number(tokens[1]);
```

